#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119710 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119890 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d503d5d-ee8f-57a2-a6ef-b5b05d5e8ae4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Rectangular Solid Given Its Dimensions"}] :question/id #uuid "78d0bc32-ce61-5c58-a31a-bf3b0cc55761" :question/math-academy-id "e-8972" :question/problem "What is the volume of a rectangular solid that has length, width, and height of $5 \\: \\textrm{m},$ $\\sqrt3 \\: \\textrm{m},$ and $\\sqrt6 \\: \\textrm{m},$ respectively?" :question/worked-solution "We can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV = lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=5 \\, \\textrm{m}, \\qquad w=\\sqrt3 \\, \\textrm{m}, \\qquad h=\\sqrt6 \\, \\textrm{m}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nV = 5 \\cdot \\sqrt3 \\cdot \\sqrt6 = 5\\sqrt{18} = 15\\sqrt2 \\: \\textrm{m}^3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119711 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119891 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a97dc9e3-b5a4-5913-94c3-aea43e639ce8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Dimension of a Rectangular Solid Given Its Volume and Some Other Dimensions"}] :question/id #uuid "35043b46-40e9-51c4-8676-ad7a81763aae" :question/math-academy-id "e-8973" :question/problem "Determine the height of the rectangular solid below given that its volume is $700\\:\\textrm{cm}^3.$\n\n![](images/8a/8a232f69c9c6abbffcb2272d4fbd237c644273826fb46dd5742bdc07d89544cb.png)" :question/worked-solution "We can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV = lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nV = 700, \\qquad l=14, \\qquad w=10\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}700 & =14\\cdot 10\\cdot h \\\\ 700 & =140h \\\\ h & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the height is $5\\:\\textrm{cm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119712 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119892 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba5bf1d9-f6e2-5494-91fd-31c20d7fa09b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Rectangular Solid: Word Problems"}] :question/id #uuid "3528ee00-01a7-5c77-af81-50d53b5fa849" :question/math-academy-id "e-8974" :question/problem "The diagram below shows a carton of orange juice. One-third of the carton is filled with juice, forming a cube. Find the volume of the empty space in the carton.\n\n![](images/90/90280dd78d285df5dc798c3ec90b7fb47a72414f2934d36885eb9d65fd7584fd.png)" :question/worked-solution "The orange juice in the carton creates a cube. Since the height of the juice is $9\\,\\textrm{cm},$ the side length of the cube is also $9\\,\\textrm{cm}.$\n\nThe height of $9 \\: \\textrm{cm}$ shown in the diagram represents a third of the carton's height. Therefore, the height of the carton is\n\n$$\n3 \\cdot 9 = 27 \\: \\textrm{cm}.\n$$\n\nThe empty space in the carton is a rectangular prism that is $9\\:\\textrm{cm}$ long, $9\\:\\textrm{cm}$ wide, and $27 - 9 = 18\\:\\textrm{cm}$ high.\n\nWe can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV = lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=9\\,\\textrm{cm}, \\qquad w=9\\,\\textrm{cm}, \\qquad h=18\\,\\textrm{cm}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nV = 9 \\cdot 9 \\cdot 18 = 1\\,458\\:\\textrm{cm}^3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that there is $1\\,458 \\: \\textrm{cm}^3$ of empty space in the carton."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120059 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119890 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d503d5d-ee8f-57a2-a6ef-b5b05d5e8ae4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Rectangular Solid Given Its Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7581ffc-6bb7-544d-aed6-c058c9601b42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72cm^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116562} {:answer/id #uuid "dedb4ba7-70a6-5ca5-9649-a03563ac510a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "144cm^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116563} {:answer/id #uuid "fad4dcd9-99d1-55d3-bf84-0d2ae48949b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "216cm^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116564} {:answer/id #uuid "2e50e361-5b5f-58b6-b0fc-96a58f51b2ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "168cm^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116565} {:answer/id #uuid "5096ed6a-9a5b-5ea3-860a-85f4b4794a8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{46}cm^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116566}] :answer-field/id #uuid "0489df66-7960-57e6-a30a-8acdc1bb55e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116561}] :question/id #uuid "8fe88d19-ff5a-5450-88e5-cd25bb5447f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-10227" :question/problem "What is the volume of a rectangular solid that has length, width, and height of $12cm$, $2cm$, and $6cm$, respectively?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540046 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119890 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d503d5d-ee8f-57a2-a6ef-b5b05d5e8ae4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Rectangular Solid Given Its Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72cc8687-cff9-5656-adb4-2b4961a69b57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\sqrt{6}\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539671} {:answer/id #uuid "be3f41bd-e03f-5f3c-adf5-43aca87d9777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539811} {:answer/id #uuid "d6662e26-2cf3-52e8-883d-f629f99e8a5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539845} {:answer/id #uuid "f5f2a638-a6db-5c93-b667-0d33daf6af55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\sqrt{6}\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539891} {:answer/id #uuid "fde1b598-50a6-581f-af9e-fe3b828f8b00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5f2a638-a6db-5c93-b667-0d33daf6af55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\sqrt{6}\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539891} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ad8f5b3-de32-550c-bc2b-1bd72fc02a0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539945}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3d05a680-5939-5ca9-9607-1df6158bf7b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-107606" :question/problem "What is the volume of a rectangular solid that has length, width, and height of $2\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m},$ $4\\,\\text{m},$ and $3\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m},$ respectively?" :question/worked-solution "We can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=2\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m},\\,w=4\\,\\text{m},\\,h=3\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nV=2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3}=24\\sqrt{6}\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119892 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba5bf1d9-f6e2-5494-91fd-31c20d7fa09b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Rectangular Solid: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04a735cc-2bb5-57f8-afb8-bf8a9f6cfe7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,400\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539487} {:answer/id #uuid "253a500f-10a7-5a2b-9a1d-48a97e3d0acb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "720\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539552} {:answer/id #uuid "2db94192-9608-59d6-be5f-b026801ae9ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,040\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539564} {:answer/id #uuid "a7c962e9-6e8e-5b95-b1f4-d86b14823f96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "640\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539762} {:answer/id #uuid "cb4cf501-4a8b-53d9-ba1c-97b7ebf0dc55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,480\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb4cf501-4a8b-53d9-ba1c-97b7ebf0dc55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,480\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539827} :answer-field/id #uuid "60d097f1-bd2b-5eac-9e0c-c6fa3b7f0885" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90edfdf5-24c3-54cd-8862-63c978f95f47" :question/math-academy-id "q-118872" :question/problem "A person has seven identical boxes in the form of a rectangular solid. Each box is $10\\,\\text{in}$ long, $8\\,\\text{in}$ wide, and $8\\,\\text{in}$ high. What is the total combined volume of the boxes?" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the volume of one box.\n\nWe can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=10,\\,w=8,\\,h=8\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V=10\\cdot 8\\cdot 8=640\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the total volume of the seven storage boxes is\n\n$$\n640\\cdot 7=4\\,480\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540102 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119892 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba5bf1d9-f6e2-5494-91fd-31c20d7fa09b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Rectangular Solid: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15b438ae-a475-5594-ad18-73d79bb97fd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38\\,400\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539523} {:answer/id #uuid "3aa5ef76-016b-5b8c-a1bf-7bbd48e16bf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,400\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539587} {:answer/id #uuid "3c929f1b-223c-53e1-a752-772c1da2087e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,000\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539590} {:answer/id #uuid "4161ce64-ccaa-5a03-9428-ac5e7b833fc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64\\,000\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539598} {:answer/id #uuid "ca2f13e7-3f99-5d2e-8c4c-1840ccbbf980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48\\,000\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca2f13e7-3f99-5d2e-8c4c-1840ccbbf980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48\\,000\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539825} :answer-field/id #uuid "187877f5-c38d-5e21-86e6-44ed4b5fbfcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539930}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e195bf20-65ce-5bd5-85a8-c18879f5cecb" :question/math-academy-id "q-118873" :question/problem "A shipping company delivered six identical packages in the form of a rectangular prism. Each package is $40\\,\\text{cm}$ long, $20\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, and $10\\,\\text{cm}$ high. What is the total combined volume of the packages?" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the volume of one package.\n\nWe can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=40,\\,w=20,\\,h=10\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V=40\\cdot 20\\cdot 10=8\\,000\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the total volume of the six packages is\n\n$$\n8\\,000\\cdot 6=48\\,000\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.\n$$"}]}
